            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0095" n="83" xml:id="pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859.85/703: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-15T19:00:00-04:00">August 15, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Your 278, July 26. All immobilized Danish vessels in American and Philippine
                    Island ports have been requisitioned.</p>
                <p>The act authorizing such acquisition of foreign merchant vessels provides that
                    just compensation shall be determined and made to the owners.</p>
                <p>There is no question that this Government’s right to do this exists under
                    international law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
